ork.kernel.org/patch/9184819/)  [The fix - If someone in Linux sets the duty cycle of the PWM and the PWM is currently disabled, it should stay disabled.]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53810 TEST=Debug prints  Change-Id: I3d40598e56a29898662448886ae6c3c00ab0d8cd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/353480 Commit-Ready: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="353480" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/80/353480/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3456962d93374d31985d1ec951a2147c8168d308" commit="ef8a1d849416317daa873390182cea5e2614e5f7" commit_message="pre-upload.py: run basic source checks on .{policy,conf} files  Add a few other types of text files to the common file extensions to check for basic issues, like old license headers.  BUG=none TEST=run presubmit checks on my seccomp policies with old license text TEST=`./pre-upload_unittest.py` passes  Change-Id: I3456962d93374d31985d1ec951a2147c8168d308 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/353163 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="353163" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/repohooks" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/repohooks" ref="refs/changes/63/353163/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic7dec75bc14f81b534b90a8e4f93b0fc0885900c" commit="ad899cc64a8901f23ff720280d16a82dcd7ec9bb" commit_message="libseccomp: upgraded package to upstream  Upgraded sys-libs/libseccomp to version 